{
  "_comment": [
    "Which permission asks an approval would AUTHORIZE A WRITE for — the one",
    "reading the box and the browser must make identically.",
    "",
    "The box gates a relayed `allow` on it (`mirror._authorizes_a_write`) and the",
    "browser decides whether to OFFER that allow on it (`CloudDataSource.mayAllow`).",
    "Two spellings of one rule, in two languages, so the cases live here and both",
    "sides are driven over them: `apps/cli/tests/cloud/test_cloud_relay_guard.py`",
    "and `apps/web/src/tests/pages/workspace/chat/writeClassAsks.test.ts`.",
    "",
    "The rule: the classifier's verdict decides when it gave one, because the kind",
    "alone cannot — `shell` is the canonical kind of every command, so a kind-first",
    "answer makes `ls` as much a write as `rm`. ONLY a positive `read` excuses an",
    "ask. A verdict that is missing or empty leaves the KIND to answer; a verdict",
    "that is a word — any word — is not a read, and is a write.",
    "",
    "`effect` absent means the ask carried no classified subject at all. `memory`",
    "and a word neither side knows are here because the browser folds the wire",
    "before it reads it, and a fold with no slot for a word used to drop it — which",
    "turned a verdict the box was calling a write into 'no verdict' one step later."
  ],
  "write_class_kinds": ["edit", "external", "shell", "task"],
